.TH TRN 1 2000-1月 "open_modules" "open_modules"
.SH NAME
open_modules \- read the WGCNA module map sidecar cache that was written by `write_bicor`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIopen_modules(\fBrepo\fR as string, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
read the WGCNA module map sidecar cache that was written by `write_bicor`
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBrepo\fB \fR\- 
 the same data repository directory that was passed to `write_bicor`
 (reads `{repo}/modules.dat`).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the cached module map object, or Nothing when the cache file does not exist
 (in that case `build_grn` will fall back to running the WGCNA blockwise
 module detection and write the cache automatically).
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
pass the returned object to `build_grn` via the `modules` parameter
 to skip the WGCNA blockwise module detection. Note that the cache carries a
 fingerprint (gene id row order + WGCNA configuration); when it does not match
 the current data, `build_grn` will ignore it and rebuild automatically.
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
let modules = open_modules("Z:/hsa_mat");
 let grn = WGCNA::build_grn(hsa, TF$Ensembl, opts, bicor = bicor, modules = modules);
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
TRN
